You might be able to write a plugin that creates a file whenever email
is received and make nethack's code read from it. You could have it
put in only the from and subject lines, since you can always alt-tab
and read it in outlook. For webmail, you could write a simple script
with wget and parse out the web page, writing a message when you see a
"new mail" string (you'd have to install cygwin, but you've probably
done that already).

The flipside is, last I checked, outlook didn't have bultin spam
filters, so the mail daemon might get very annoying. Also, if you have
friends who send you HTML-formatted email, you'll be pretty much
forced to read it in outlook rather than nethack.

It might be easier to use mozilla for all this. The spam filters will
help you, for one thing. I'd have to check what their format for their
mailbox is, but even if nethack can't read it directly, I have a
feeling that writing a plugin might be easier.



