Ok, maybe you don't have cygwin installed. Go to cygwin.com. In the
installer make sure you selected the X server and ssh. You might want
windowmaker too. Also make sure you have X forwarding enabled in your
sshd in you linux box. Then you should be able to do startx on your
windows machine, ssh -X linux, and run everything on a real xterm, or
use whetever GUI you want for nethack. Granted, this won't help with
the mail daemon.

Maybe cygwin can install pine, and nethack could read from its
directory. I'd have to check.



In the end,this is a neat feature, but not very useful, in thesse days
of multitasking and guis. You can be playing nethack, and when you
hear your email notification sound, switch to your mail reader, read,
and switch back. Still, it might be neat to try it.

Or, even more disruptive,  hook it up to an IM program :)

